  "limits": [
    "Finite trusted private-peer TCP histories with three/five nodes and initial observers. No native Kafka Fetch/FetchSnapshot/KRaft compatibility or production readiness is established; KL11-70 remains separate.",
    "Numeric fixed routes perform no DNS admissions. Configured routes do not authorize unknown voting directories; raw replay supplies membership authority. Private CRC framing requires an isolated trusted network and supplies no peer authentication.",
    "Bounded frames, records, image chunks, queues, transport charges and task ownership are verified from actual settings and constructed RAII high-water counters. Acquired-but-unpublished permits, allocator overhead, process RSS and OS socket buffers are excluded.",
    "Clock epochs stay local to each owner process and parent proxy. Exact raw prefixes bridge restarts. Packet reads, successful forwarding writes and consumed owner acknowledgements are distinct facts; dropped/delayed/unconsumed bytes never count as commit authority.",
    "Controlled process exits88 are parent-waited crashes, not joined shutdowns. Every successful TCP owner/supervisor shutdown restores permits, closes its listener and joins network workers. The standalone cancellation test also rebinds its listener.",
    "Direct owner controls use intentional one/sixteen-slot channels and no network workers. Their typed inputs are not counted as TCP packets. Eight abandoned vote correlations, a real late Append ACK and an old timeout are independently checked without durable mutation.",
    "All latest-stable whole-broker default/all tests, strict Clippy, formatting and rustdoc checks pass. These checks do not independently qualify other security/protocol drafts merely because their local tests run.",
    "Historical Rust1.85 syntax receipts remain unchanged; current execution uses stable1.99.0 only. Failed provenance/checker attempts and the Fetch admission-probe timeout remain retained. That older failed Fetch harness was overwritten before ELF retention; its exact source and command failure are retained, and no successful qualification is transferred from it.",
    "The Fetch shutdown test now observes the pending handler before probing its single data slot. Its previous polling probe could itself take admission and close the socket handler; no transport product behavior or deadline was changed.",
    "No performance ranking, soak duration, hostile network, allocator/RSS or exhaustive consensus proof follows from these finite captures."
  ],
